**Decision 2026-11-21 (main agent), on the review's finding 1:** the cap drops from 96 KiB to 48 KiB (49,152 bytes).

**Why:** Claude Code saves a text reply over 50,000 characters to a file, so a cut 96 KiB reply never reaches the agent's context. 48 KiB of bytes is at most 49,152 characters, marker included, and it also stays well under Claude Code's token limit for MCP output. A client-specific `_meta` limit was rejected: unreagent serves other MCP clients too, and one plain cap is simpler.

